@startuml reconciliation

title ExternalDNS reconciliation through Universal DDI

participant "Kubernetes API" as Kubernetes
participant "ExternalDNS" as ExternalDNS
participant "UDDI webhook\nlocalhost:8888" as Webhook
participant "Universal DDI\nPortal API" as Portal

== Provider initialization ==

ExternalDNS -> Webhook: GET /
Webhook --> ExternalDNS: Configured domain filter

== Reconciliation ==

loop Every synchronization interval
    ExternalDNS -> Kubernetes: Read configured sources
    Kubernetes --> ExternalDNS: Services, Ingresses, HTTPRoutes,\nand other resources
    ExternalDNS -> ExternalDNS: Build desired endpoints

    ExternalDNS -> Webhook: GET /records

    opt Zone cache has expired
        Webhook -> Portal: List cloud-primary zones\nin the configured view
        Portal --> Webhook: Authoritative zones
        Webhook -> Webhook: Apply domain and zone filters
    end

    loop For each allowed zone
        Webhook -> Portal: List DNS records
        Portal --> Webhook: Zone records
    end

    Webhook -> Webhook: Group UDDI records into\nExternalDNS endpoints
    Webhook --> ExternalDNS: Current endpoints

    ExternalDNS -> Webhook: POST /adjustendpoints\nwith desired endpoints
    Webhook -> Webhook: Drop unsupported types, normalize TXT values,\nand apply the default TTL
    Webhook --> ExternalDNS: Adjusted endpoints

    ExternalDNS -> ExternalDNS: Apply TXT ownership and\nbuild the change plan

    alt Changes are required
        ExternalDNS -> Webhook: POST /records\nwith create, update, and delete changes
        Webhook -> Webhook: Select the longest-matching zone,\nexpand targets, and order operations

        loop For each record operation
            Webhook -> Portal: Create, update, or delete one record
            Portal --> Webhook: Operation result
        end

        Webhook --> ExternalDNS: Change result
    else No changes are required
        ExternalDNS -> ExternalDNS: Finish synchronization
    end
end

note over ExternalDNS, Webhook
DNS queries do not pass through
ExternalDNS or the webhook.
end note

@enduml
